AUREUS-000 — DOCUMENT 30

GOVERNANCE

Status: Constitutional Document

---

Purpose

This document establishes how Aureus is governed.

Governance exists to preserve the Mission, protect the rights of every member, uphold this Constitution, and ensure that authority is exercised as stewardship rather than power.

Every office within Aureus exists to serve the institution.

The institution exists to serve people.

---

Section 1 — Constitutional Authority

This Constitution is the supreme governing authority of Aureus.

Every office, policy, technology, agreement, and institutional decision shall conform to this Constitution.

No authority exists beyond that granted by this Constitution.

---

Section 2 — The Managing Member

During the Founding Phase, Aureus operates as a founder-managed limited liability company.

The Managing Member serves as the chief executive officer of the organization and bears ultimate responsibility for the faithful operation of Aureus under this Constitution.

The Managing Member is bound by this Constitution and possesses no authority to suspend or disregard it.

---

Section 3 — Stewardship of Authority

Authority within Aureus is held in trust.

Every leader, steward, employee, volunteer, contractor, and representative shall exercise authority:

- with integrity;
- with humility;
- for the benefit of members;
- consistent with this Constitution.

Authority exists to serve.

It shall never become an end in itself.

---

Section 4 — Delegation

The Managing Member may delegate operational responsibilities.

Delegation transfers responsibility for execution.

It does not transfer constitutional accountability.

Those exercising delegated authority remain accountable to this Constitution.

---

Section 5 — Constitutional Decision-Making

Institutional decisions shall be guided by:

- the Mission;
- the Eternal Principles;
- the Rights of Every Member;
- the long-term flourishing of people;
- faithful stewardship of institutional resources.

When these considerations appear to conflict, decision-makers shall seek the interpretation that best preserves the Constitution as a whole.

---

Section 6 — Transparency

Aureus shall conduct its governance with transparency whenever consistent with member privacy, safety, and applicable law.

Significant constitutional decisions shall be documented.

Material amendments and constitutional interpretations shall be made publicly available.

Transparency strengthens trust.

---

Section 7 — Institutional Accountability

Every office of Aureus remains accountable under this Constitution.

No office, leader, or governing body is exempt from constitutional review.

Constitutional concerns shall be addressed according to the procedures established by this Constitution.

---

Section 8 — Transition to Permanent Governance

The Founding Phase is intended to establish Aureus as a stable constitutional institution.

When Aureus demonstrates constitutional maturity, governance responsibilities shall transition to the permanent constitutional structure established by this Constitution.

The transition shall occur only through the procedures provided by this Constitution and shall preserve the Mission, the Eternal Principles, and the Rights of Every Member.

---

Section 9 — Constitutional Continuity

Changes in leadership, ownership, organizational structure, or technology shall not diminish the constitutional obligations of Aureus.

The institution shall remain faithful to this Constitution throughout every period of transition.

---

Section 10 — Stewardship Across Generations

Governance exists not merely to lead the present generation but to preserve Aureus for those yet to come.

Every generation inherits the institution in trust.

Every generation bears the responsibility to leave it more trustworthy, more faithful, and more capable of helping people flourish than it was received.

Every exercise of governance shall ultimately answer one question:

"Does this decision strengthen Aureus' ability to help people flourish—forever?"